# device-layer-0021.
# Biometrics: asking the person to prove it is them with the face or the finger the device knows, through the
# platform's own sheet: LocalAuthentication (Face ID, Touch ID) on iOS and macOS, BiometricPrompt on Android. A browser,
# a desktop JVM and a Rust program have none to ask.
#
#   biometric-kind         the hardware: face, fingerprint, none (there is none), or unavailable (nothing here can
#                          say). Whether anything is enrolled is authenticate's `not-enrolled`. Never shows anything
#   authenticate(reason)   passed, failed (no match, or the person cancelled), not-enrolled, or unavailable. `reason`
#                          is the line the platform's sheet shows
#
# A host with no such capability (the server, the memory host) answers `unavailable`. Every answer is text from the
# closed set above, so an app compares strings and no platform enum ever reaches it.

load ./native/{platform}/biometric
  find read-biometric-kind
  find ask-biometric

task biometric-kind
  like text
  send back
    call read-biometric-kind

task authenticate
  take reason, like text
  like text
  send back
    call ask-biometric
      read reason
